d 'HILLPLOT': module to draw Hill plots for distribution tails 
d
d  Data are for a variable x with distribution function F(x).
d Ordered values are labelled x_(1) >= ... >= x_(n).  Note that
d indexing here is the reverse of a more common convention. Given
d some slowly varying function L(x):  if pr(X > x) = 1 - F(x) =
d L(x) x^-alpha for large x and alpha > 0, then for k < n, the tail
d index alpha can be estimated by the reciprocal of (1 / k) SUM [
d log x_(i) / x_(k+1) ]. hillplot plots estimates of alpha versus k
d and optionally estimates of alpha versus log(k / n) = log(1 -
d F(x)). This is not the Hill plot as known in biochemistry and
d pharmacology. The command is an updated version of that discussed
d at the 6th London Stata meeting in 2000. 
d
d KW: Hill plot
d KW: distributions
d KW: graphics
d KW: extremes
d
d Requires: Stata version 8.2
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261025
d
d Author: Nicholas J. Cox, Durham University
d Support: email N.J.Cox@@durham.ac.uk
d
f hillplot.ado
f hillplot.sthlp
